        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0367" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg271"/>

                <head>No. 214.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Bassett.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 16,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 103.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatches numbered 120, 122, and 123
                    have been received. For the views of this Department respecting the indignity
                    offered to the consular officer of the United States at Saint Marc, to which you
                    revert in your dispatch No. 123, you are referred to my instruction No. 101, of
                    the 3d instant.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
